[[Image:Old Soar Manor3.jpg|300px|thumb|Old Soar Manor]]
'''Old Soar Manor''' is an [[English Heritage]] property, owned and maintained by the [[National Trust]]. Located near [[Plaxtol]], [[Kent]], England, it is a small 13th century stone [[manor house]]. It is [[Listed building#England and Wales|listed Grade I]] on the [[National Heritage List for England]].<ref name=NHLEManor>{{NHLE|num=1281122|desc=Old Soar, Plaxtol|access-date=14 April 2019|mode=cs2}}</ref>

Built in 1290, the manor originally belonged to the Culpepper family. The centre of the house was originally the great hall but this no longer exists, as it was demolished in 1780 and replaced with the red-brick farmhouse on the site. The farmhouse is Grade II listed.<ref name=NHLEFarm>{{NHLE|num=1072691|desc=Old Soar Farmhouse, Plaxtol|access-date=14 April 2019|mode=cs2}}</ref><ref name="auto">{{Cite web|url=https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/whats-on/|title=What's On|website=[[English Heritage]]|accessdate=22 December 2024}}</ref>  Visitors today can see the [[Solar (room)|solar]], [[latrine]] and chapel which remain.<ref name="auto"/>

