'''One Tree Hill and Bitchet Common''' is a {{convert| 79.2 |ha|acre|abbr=off|adj=on}} biological [[Site of Special Scientific Interest]] east of [[Sevenoaks]] in [[Kent]].<ref name=dsv>{{cite web|url=  https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/SiteDetail.aspx?SiteCode=S1000317&SiteName=bitchet&countyCode=&responsiblePerson=&SeaArea=&IFCAArea= |title=Designated Sites View: One Tree Hill and Bitchet Common  | series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|access-date =  21 February 2018}}</ref><ref name=map>{{cite web|url=http://magic.defra.gov.uk/MagicMap.aspx?startTopic=Designations&activelayer=sssiIndex&query=HYPERLINK%3D%271000317%27 |title=Map of One Tree Hill and Bitchet Common|series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|access-date=  21 February 2018}}</ref> It is in [[Kent Downs]] [[Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty]]<ref name=onecite>{{cite web|url=  https://designatedsites.naturalengland.org.uk/PDFsForWeb/Citation/1000317.pdf |title=One Tree Hill and Bitchet Common citation|series= Sites of Special Scientific Interest|publisher=Natural England|access-date=   21 February 2018}}</ref> and One Tree Hill is managed by the [[National Trust]]<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/one-tree-hill|title=One Tree Hill|publisher=National Trust|access-date=17 January 2018|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180118122450/https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/one-tree-hill|archive-date=18 January 2018}}</ref>

This site has mixed woodland on the [[Lower Greensand]], some of it of ancient origin. The habitats are varied, including acidic soils on Bitchet Common and damp, [[base-rich]] soils in Martins Wood. There are several rare plants and invertebrates.<ref name=onecite/>

The site is in several blocks crossed by public footpaths.

